      ],
      "extract": "[]{#plancherel label=\"plancherel\"} The random variable we wish to study is $T_n(\\lambda) = \\frac{\\sqrt{n \\choose 2} \\chi^{\\lambda}(12)}{dim(\\lambda)}$ where $\\lambda$ is chosen from the Plancherel measure of the symmetric group $S_n$. To begin we write $T_n$ as a sum of other random variables. For this we need Kerov's growth process on partitions [@K2]; this has a natural generalization to arbitrary finite groups",
      "extractCut": true
